  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the visual material of the dead monkey",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any deictic element (like 'me', 'you') in the text or visual material. However, the meme's overall intent and the visual-textual composition create an implicit projection where the user is positioned as the observer of the disturbing scene, thereby internalizing or being confronted with the hateful stereotype. The user is projected onto the visual material (the dead monkey with blood) as the primary object of the meme's dehumanizing message, which is meant to evoke disgust and reinforce racial prejudice. The user is also implicitly projected onto the textual material ('monkey blood') as the label that categorizes and defines the visual entity, reinforcing the racist trope.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
